From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: propagate scan dispatch errors

mt_cfg80211_ops_scan() returns zero even when dispatch fails before the
driver accepts the request. cfg80211 then waits for a completion that
cannot arrive.

The callback now returns the dispatch result so cfg80211 can release
rejected requests. This requires the driver scan callback to return zero
after accepting a request, including when it reports an aborted scan
during startup. Propagating a negative return after that notification
would submit the same request to both completion and rejection cleanup.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_osal_cfg80211.c
+++ b/mt_osal_cfg80211.c
@@ -2379,10 +2379,9 @@ static int mt_cfg80211_ops_scan(
 	MT_DEBUG_TRACE("80211> %s ==>\n", pNdev->name);
 	ctrl_data_ptr->uint_val = pWdev->iftype;
 	ctrl_data_ptr->data = pRequest;
-	mt_cfg80211_ops_ctrl(wiphy, pNdev, mtk_ops_scan,
+	return mt_cfg80211_ops_ctrl(wiphy, pNdev, mtk_ops_scan,
 			ctrl_data_ptr, sizeof(struct mt_cfg80211_vndr_ctrl));
 
-	return 0;
 }
 
 static void mt_cfg80211_ops_abort_scan(
